Grep command

global regular expression print

grep is useful command to search for matching pattern in a file

grep [options] "pattern" [file]

Pattern: The string or regular expression (regex) you are hunting for.
File: The target text file. If omitted, grep reads from standard input (via pipes |).

In shell scripts, grep behaves like a boolean check because of its Exit Status Codes:
• 0: Success (The pattern was found).
• 1: Failure (The pattern was not found).
• 2: Error (e.g., file not found or syntax error).


-i	Case-insensitive	Ensures the script doesn't break if a log contains "Error", "error", or "ERROR".
